cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Catigraphy: an interactive CT atlas of the domestic cat"
message: "If you use this software or its teaching material, please cite it as below, and cite the source scans as recorded in public/ATTRIBUTION.md."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sofi-Mahmudi
    given-names: Ahmad
    email: ahmad.pub@gmail.com
    alias: choxos
repository-code: "https://github.com/choxos/catigraphy"
abstract: >-
  An interactive browser atlas of domestic cat anatomy built from twelve
  computed tomography series of one specimen published on MorphoSource by
  3D Anatomy Studios. Each series is rebuilt as a bone surface by marching
  cubes on the thresholded volume and is served together with the volume
  itself, which the browser reslices in three planes with selectable
  windows. The skull carries fifteen named landmarks placed against the
  midsagittal slice; every region carries a written note. The two whole body
  series overlap along the lumbar spine and share five metal fiducials, so
  they are registered and fused into one whole skeleton, agreeing to a median
  of 0.28 mm on bone. The ten regional series share no frame of reference
  with anything, so the rest of the atlas is regional, and the bones within a
  region are not segmented from one another. It is an educational reference
  and is not intended for diagnosis.
keywords:
  - feline anatomy
  - veterinary anatomy
  - comparative anatomy
  - computed tomography
  - 3D visualization
  - open educational resources
license: MIT
